From: DockSeed <dockseed@proton.me>
Subject: [PATCH] drm: a733: dp: link training -- CR and EQ against drm_dp_helper, with fallback

[Recipe cut: regenerated: context only, the removed debugfs knobs of earlier
patches are not touched here.]

The last piece of the pixel path that was still a shell script. As of
2026-08-19 the clocks, TCON_TV1 and the eDP video stream are driver code and
HW-proven -- a 1920x1200 picture came up from
`clk-sunxi-ng-a733-video-plls-and-edp-tv-pixel-clock`,
`arm64-dts-a733-tcon-tv1-and-the-dp-phy-pad-window`,
`drm-a733-tcon-tv1-timing-generator-and-video-source` and
`drm-a733-dp-the-main-video-stream` alone --
with a by-hand shell script still doing the training in between.

WHAT THE DRM CORE ALREADY DOES, AND WHAT IT DOES NOT
-----------------------------------------------------

Checked before writing anything, because "call the core, write almost nothing"
would have been the right answer if it were true. It is not:

  drivers/gpu/drm/display/drm_dp_helper.c provides PREDICATES and DELAYS --
  drm_dp_clock_recovery_ok(), drm_dp_channel_eq_ok(),
  drm_dp_get_adjust_request_voltage/pre_emphasis(),
  drm_dp_dpcd_read_link_status(), drm_dp_link_train_clock_recovery_delay(),
  drm_dp_link_train_channel_eq_delay(), drm_dp_read_*_delay(), the LTTPR
  helpers, drm_dp_link_rate_to_bw_code(), drm_dp_max_link_rate/lane_count(),
  drm_dp_tps3_supported(), drm_dp_enhanced_frame_cap().

  It does NOT provide a state machine. There is no generic drm_dp_link_train().
  Fourteen drivers in 6.18.36 each write their own CR/EQ loop, and the "five
  attempts at an unchanged voltage swing" rule of DP 1.4 section 3.5.1.2.2 is
  implemented NINE times in nine different ways -- the number 5 does not appear
  in a single core header (grep MAX_TRAINING_TRIES/voltage_tries include/drm/
  returns nothing).

⚠ A trap worth naming: drm_dp_link_train() DOES exist, at
drivers/gpu/drm/tegra/dp.c:792, together with a whole drm_dp_link_* family that
looks generic. It is Tegra-private -- zero EXPORT_SYMBOL in that file -- and its
loops are `for (repeat = 1; repeat < 5; repeat++)` with no per-voltage counter at
all. Not callable, and not a model.

So: every helper the core has is called here and none is open-coded. The loop
shape follows zynqmp_dp_link_train() (drivers/gpu/drm/xlnx/zynqmp_dp.c:694-1010)
and the fallback ladder follows hibmc_dp_link_training()
(drivers/gpu/drm/hisilicon/hibmc/dp/dp_link.c:310-420) -- the two cleanest of
the fourteen, both of which use the core predicates throughout.

AND NOTHING UPSTREAM TARGETS ALLWINNER DP
------------------------------------------

Verified rather than inherited from an earlier note: drivers/gpu/drm/sun4i/ has
no DisplayPort at all (its only "edp" hits are a reset-line NAME in
sun4i_tcon.c:1145,1151), there is no allwinner DP/eDP binding in
Documentation/devicetree/bindings/display/, and every allwinner PHY binding is
USB or MIPI-DPHY. dw-dp.c is a Synopsys DesignWare library with exactly one
consumer, dw_dp-rockchip.c, bound to "rockchip,rk3588-dp" -- different IP from
the Trilinear core at 0x05740000, so its registers do not apply here. Its loop
is also unbounded in CR, has no lane fallback, and leaves a union
phy_configure_opts uninitialised on the stack (dw-dp.c:559).

WHERE THE VENDOR DRIVER DIFFERS, AND WHAT THIS PATCH DOES
---------------------------------------------------------

The following are points where the vendor driver differs from what this
patch does:

